      },
      "worked": "The stated conditions make both logarithm bases valid and the denominator nonzero. Change the base to $a$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{a^x}(b)&=\\frac{\\log_a(b)}{\\log_a(a^x)}\\\\\\log_{a^x}(b)&=\\frac{\\log_a(b)}{x\\log_a(a)}\\\\\\log_{a^x}(b)&=\\frac{\\log_a(b)}{x}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
